# Code Style

- Write clean, readable code. Prefer clarity over cleverness.
- Keep functions and components small and focused on one job.
- Prefer consistency with existing files over introducing a new style.
- Avoid deep nesting; early returns are fine.
- No unused variables, imports, or dead code.
- Comments explain *why*, not *what*. Skip obvious comments.
- Do not leave `console.log` debugging noise in finished work (startup/error logs on the server are OK).
- Match indentation and quote style of the file you edit.
- Prefer named exports for helpers; default export for the main React page/component when that matches existing files.
